CORE INDIAN RAILWAYS STATUTORY RULEBOOKS IN YOUR KNOWLEDGE BASE:
1. IRPWM (Indian Railways Permanent Way Manual 2020):
   - Para 268 & 523: Action on USFD ultrasonic flaw detection.
     * IMR (Immediate Marked Rail): Immediate imposition of TSR 30 km/h, emergency joggled fishplates with two clamps, rail renewal within 24 hours.
     * IMRW (Immediate Marked Rail Weld): TSR 30 km/h, joggled fishplate with clamps, replace weld within 24 hours.
     * REM (Rail Early Marked) / OBS (Observed): USFD re-testing within 15-30 days under periodic monitoring.
   - Para 607 & 608: Deep screening of ballast using BCM. Initial speed 20 km/h after 1st round tamping, 45 km/h after 2nd round, 75 km/h after 3rd round, and section speed (110-130 km/h) after 4th round tamping and stabilization by Dynamic Track Stabilizer (DTS).
   - Para 812-817: LWR / CWR Track Temperature limits. Hot weather patrolling starts when rail temp Tr > Td + 20°C (e.g. 40°C). Emergency hot weather patrolling when Tr > Td + 25°C (46°C). Cold weather patrolling when Tr < Td - 30°C. De-stressing required before peak summer/winter.
   - Para 412: Minimum distance of AT weld from fishplate hole is 100 mm; clearance between weld and sleeper is 100 mm. Minimum rail cushion is 300 mm PSC for LWR/CWR track.

2. IRSEM (Indian Railways Signal Engineering Manual):
   - Track circuit insulation resistance: Glued insulated rail joints (GJ) must maintain minimum resistance > 1000 ohms (wet condition) and > 2000 ohms (dry condition).
   - Point Machine tolerances: Point detector contacts must open when point is obstructed by a 3.5 mm test gauge at facing point lock (FPL). Facing point switch detection clearance: 1.5 mm to 3.5 mm.
   - Signal Sighting Distances: Distant Signal sighting distance min 1000 m; Home Signal sighting distance min 600 m on absolute block lines.
   - Disconnection Memo: Form S&T (T) 1 is legally mandatory before opening point machines, relay rooms, or track circuits.

